xanthian.

[*] It amuses me that Derek Ray can claim both that
a sample of 1000 NAO games would suffice _fully_[**]
to provide the statistics _he_ needs for an
estimate, while at the very same time insisting that
Dr. Kassner's experience playing 200 games of
NetHack provides _no basis whatever_ for an
estimate.

The title for that kind of thinking is "innumerate".

[**] Well, no it wouldn't. With a sample of 1000,
_one_ extinctionist game, with its many thousands of
additional kills and so chances of dropping items
such as potions, would be able to skew the data
significantly, but probably less than 1 game in 1000
is played _as_ an extinctionist game, so whether an
extinctionist game did or did not occur in a sample
would make the statistics very different.

Similar, though weaker arguments can be made for
speed ascensions and for pacifist games, but in the
opposite direction, many fewer than normal
monster-associated items would be expected to be
seen.

Instead of 1000 games sufficing, a sample big enough
to include a _representative number_ of
extinctionist games and a _representative number_ of
speed ascension / pacifist games would be needed to
acquire trustworthy statistics.

Even guessing how big a sample that sample would
need to be would take a lot of analysis of existing
logs for the frequency of various playing styles.




